T*
(3.1 FILTER CHAIN POSITIONING) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `JWTAuthFilter` is placed before `UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter`.) Tj
T*
(- It parses Bearer token, validates signature/expiry, and stores principal in security context.) Tj
T*
(- It sets `request.setAttribute\("clientId", subject\)` for downstream rate limiting.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.2 ACCESS MODEL) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Public: `/api/auth/**`, `/actuator/**`) Tj
T*
(- Authenticated: all other endpoints) Tj
T*
(- Admin-specific authorization enforced by route and role-based logic where configured.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.3 LOGIN FLOW) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. `AuthController` accepts credentials.) Tj
T*
(2. `AuthenticationManager` authenticates principal.) Tj
T*
(3. `JWTTokenProvider` creates signed token with role claim and expiration.) Tj
T*
(4. Token is returned to caller for subsequent protected calls.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
