() Tj
T*
(1. Check lock key `otp:lock:{identifier}` in Redis.) Tj
T*
(2. Generate random numeric OTP \(`SecureRandom`\) with configured length.) Tj
T*
(3. Hash OTP via BCrypt.) Tj
T*
(4. Persist OTP record with expiry timestamp.) Tj
T*
(5. Build and dispatch `NotificationEvent`.) Tj
T*
(6. Return success response.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.2 VERIFY OTP \(`VERIFIESOTP`\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Check lock status.) Tj
T*
(2. Fetch latest unused OTP record for identifier/channel.) Tj
T*
(3. Validate expiry.) Tj
T*
(4. Increment attempts and evaluate max-attempt threshold.) Tj
T*
(5. On threshold breach, create lock key with configured lockout TTL.) Tj
T*
(6. Compare input OTP against BCrypt hash.) Tj
T*
(7. If matched, mark record as used and return true; else return false.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.3 ERROR CONDITIONS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- No active OTP record found.) Tj
T*
(- OTP expired.) Tj
T*
(- Account currently locked due to excessive attempts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. LLD-4: IDEMPOTENT PAYMENT PROCESSING) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Primary classes:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `service/PaymentService.java`) Tj
T*
(- `controller/PaymentController.java`) Tj
T*
(- `repository/PaymentRepository.java`) Tj
T*
(- `model/Payment.java`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.1 PROCESSING STEPS \(`PROCESSPAYMENT`\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Build Redis key `payment:idem:{idempotencyKey}`.) Tj
T*
(2. If Redis key exists, return existing payment by idempotency key.) Tj
T*
(3. Else check durable existence in MySQL repository.) Tj
T*
(4. If absent, create `Payment` as `PENDING` and persist.) Tj
T*
(5. Execute gateway operation \(currently internal method placeholder\).) Tj
T*
(6. On success: set `SUCCESS`, set `processedAt`, persist, cache key in Redis with TTL.) Tj
T*
(7. On failure: set `FAILED`, persist failure reason.) Tj
T*
(8. Dispatch corresponding notification template.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.2 CONSISTENCY NOTES) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- DB unique constraint on idempotency key prevents duplicate inserts.) Tj
T*
(- Redis accelerates retries while DB remains source of truth.) Tj
T*
(- Event dispatch is asynchronous and does not block payment API response.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. LLD-5: NOTIFICATION DISPATCH) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
